105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Why do we acknowledge the land?)
/E (Why do we acknowledge the land?)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Land acknowledgments offered in post-secondary institutions originated as a practice that disrupted the erasure of Indigenous Peoples from the land and the Canadian narrative. Today, land acknowledgments have become more common, and have evolved to be a sign of respect for the land and its original Peoples. Offering a land acknowledgement is also an opportunity to express our responsibilities to the land, and to identify the kind of relationships we are striving to build. Acknowledging the land is a practice that everyone can engage in, and it can be a prompt for further action towards reconciliation. It is appropriate for this land acknowledgment to be used consistently in all printed material, especially materials that are used outside of our college community \(in student recruitment, for example\).)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
