/T (Why is terminology important?)
/E (Why is terminology important?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Using the correct terminology is not just a matter of politeness, but it is crucial for respect and accuracy. Indigenous Peoples often prefer to be referred to by the traditional name of their specific community rather than general terms. This approach acknowledges and respects the diversity and unique heritage of each community.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (By using respectful and accurate terminology, we can work towards a more inclusive and respectful dialogue between Canadian institutions and Indigenous communities.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
