127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The term "Peoples" emphasizes the collective nature of Indigenous rights, including the right to self-determination. This is crucial because self-determination is a collective right that allows Indigenous peoples to decide their own political status, economic, social, and cultural development.  This recognition is essential for respecting and protecting unique identities and ways of life.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Indigenous negotiators advocated strongly for the United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples the use of the term "Peoples" instead of "People" because it recognizes the collective rights and distinct identities of various Indigenous groups.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
